    "questionNumber": 39,
    "stem": "The White House claims that its power of enforcement _______.",
    "stemTranslation": null,
    "options": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "outweighs that held by the states.",
        "isCorrect": true,
        "analysis": "定位至第六段 S13-S14：“The White House argued that Arizona’s laws conflicted with its enforcement priorities, even if state laws complied with federal statutes to the letter. In effect, the White House claimed that it could invalidate any otherwise legitimate state law that it disagrees with.” 白宫主张即使州法一字不差地严格符合联邦法律，只要与白宫的执法优先级不一致，白宫就可以任意将其废止作废。这种霸道行径实质上是在声称联邦行政分支的执法自由裁量权可以彻底碾压、超越并凌驾于各州所拥有的执法权力（outweighs that held by the states）。",
        "vocab": [
          {
            "word": "states",
            "ipa": "",
            "meaning": "州",
            "level": "green",
            "isSelfAnnotated": false
          }
        ],
        "selfAnnotated": false
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "is established by federal statutes.",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "distractorType": "CONCEPT_DISTORTION",
        "analysis": "偷换概念与断章取义。第六段第二句说‘even if state laws complied with federal statutes’，白宫主张的是超越成文法约束的自身行政‘执法优先权（enforcement priorities）’，恰恰被法官斥为缺乏法律依据的 shocking assertion。",
        "vocab": [
          {
            "word": "dependent",
            "ipa": "[dɪˈpendənt]",
            "meaning": "依赖",
            "level": "green",
            "isSelfAnnotated": false
          }
        ],
        "selfAnnotated": false
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "is dependent on the states' support.",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "distractorType": "CONTRADICTION",
        "analysis": "正反颠倒。白宫声称自己可以随意废除不听话的合法州法，这表明它自视至高无上，绝非‘依赖各州的支持’。",
